==================================================
19. DATA FLOW REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

All rendering and editing must follow clean data flow.

Frontend public site flow:
request -> resolve tenant -> load tenant theme -> load page config -> fetch tenant content -> render ordered sections

Admin flow:
tenant admin -> edit page config/theme/content -> save tenant-scoped config -> frontend reflects changes

AI content flow:
tenant admin -> submit generation request -> AI service -> validate/store content with tenantId -> content appears in page builder/content modules

==================================================
20. WHAT TO AVOID
==================================================

You must explicitly avoid the following mistakes:

1. frontend duplication per tenant
2. hardcoded tenant switch statements across codebase
3. raw CSS text fields everywhere
4. building all imagined future sections at once
5. uncontrolled variant explosion
6. mixing page content with component structure logic
7. weak tenant isolation
8. storing email passwords
9. tightly coupling future email integration to one provider
10. breaking existing AI features during refactor
11. giant unplanned rewrite without incremental migration
12. introducing hidden regressions in current routes and APIs

